%I A049512 #29 Sep 07 2026 23:48:34
%S A049512 1,2,13,197,9312,1528634,880277970,1792432587311,13026136308914662,
%T A049512 341247348570900375431
%N A049512 Number of quasi-initially connected digraphs on n unlabeled nodes.
%C A049512 From _Sean A. Irvine_, Aug 01 2021: (Start)
%C A049512 A quasi-initially connected digraph is a digraph containing at least one vertex v such that every vertex u in the graph can either be reached from v or v can be reached from u (while obeying the directions on the edges).
%C A049512 There is no known formula. (End)
%C A049512 a(8) was computed by Burnside's lemma, grouping permutations by cycle type. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 07 2026
%H A049512 Sean A. Irvine, <a href="https://github.com/archmageirvine/joeis/blob/master/src/irvine/oeis/a049/A049512.java">Java program</a> (github)
%H A049512 V. Jovovic and G. Kilibarda, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/S0012-365X(00)00112-6">Enumeration of labeled quasi-initially connected digraphs</a>, Discrete Math., 224 (2000), 151-163.
%F A049512 a(n) = (1/n!) * Sum_{g in S_n} Fix(g), where Fix(g) is the number of quasi-initially connected digraphs fixed by g. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 07 2026
%Y A049512 Cf. A049414, A003085, A035512, A003088, A051421.
%K A049512 hard,more,nonn,changed
%O A049512 1,2
